{
    "spec_version": "v1.18",
    "identifier": "RP-AXE",
    "name": "RP-AXE: Ahistorical Xploration & Engineering",
    "abstract": "RP-1's realism stack with a lightweight, science-driven, exploration-first career replacing the RP-1 career plugin. Parts unlock free with science; engineering and exploration are the focus, not management.",
    "author": [
        "miskoltrans"
    ],
    "license": "CC-BY-NC-SA-4.0",
    "$kref": "#/ckan/github/miskoltrans/RP-AXE",
    "$vref": "#/ckan/ksp-avc",
    "tags": [
        "config",
        "career",
        "total-conversion",
        "career-scaling",
        "physics"
    ],
    "x_netkan_github": {
        "prerelease": true
    },
    "comment": "RELATIONSHIPS (generated by tools/gen_netkan.py; edit the lists there). depends = the stack AXE's configs and plugin bind to directly (RO/RSS/Kerbalism/ContractConfigurator/CustomBarnKit/RealAntennas/KSCSwitcher/Skopos, ROUtils+Harmony+MFI for AXE.dll) plus EVERY mod the tree places parts from (manifest/curated-parts.tsv): the tree is balanced against exactly that part set, and a missing one leaves nodes you pay science for and get nothing from. recommends = tools AXE integrates with when present and runs without. suggests = the author's RP-1-Express-High graphics preset (heavy; RP-AXE-Graphics-High.ckan / -Low.ckan import one in a go) and the DLCs, which CKAN cannot install (Breaking Ground carries the 28 robotics parts the tree places). Transitive deps are left to CKAN. 'Scatterer-config-default'/'-sunflare-default' on purpose: the bare virtual names have many providers and a headless resolver silently drops them. SCANsat = stock CKAN SCANsat. RP-AXE-deps.ckan is the author's full dev environment (everything here as hard deps, High graphics). Conflicts: RP-AXE replaces the RP-1 career layer and ships its own tree, simulator and RTG model.",
